{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115716",
      "title": "Getting Access to Template Elements via ViewChild",
      "lectureOrder": 132,
      "videoOrder": 126,
      "sourceHash": "751716c42bb053432f97e13d84085db91e6665e96f8c7894c493ecf94e3a0a82",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.798,
          "end": 2.61,
          "en": "[Maximilian Schwarzmuller] So you did learn quite a bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.61,
          "end": 5.97,
          "en": "about template variables already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.97,
          "end": 8.16,
          "en": "and now I wanna build up on that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.16,
          "end": 12.84,
          "en": "and use a template variable to reset that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.84,
          "end": 14.643,
          "en": "whenever it is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.54,
          "end": 17.7,
          "en": "And then building up on that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.7,
          "end": 22.41,
          "en": "I'll show you a different way of getting hold of the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.41,
          "end": 25.32,
          "en": "that's stored in the template variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.32,
          "end": 26.52,
          "en": "but let's start simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.52,
          "end": 29.52,
          "en": "Let's make sure that we get access to that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.52,
          "end": 32.19,
          "en": "through a template variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.19,
          "end": 34.56,
          "en": "To do that, you can add a template variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.56,
          "end": 36.54,
          "en": "to the form element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.54,
          "end": 37.65,
          "en": "and I'll name it form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 37.65,
          "end": 39.45,
          "en": "but of course the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 40.41,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "And if you hover over that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 45.393,
          "en": "you see that it is the DOM element, the HTMLFormElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.53,
          "end": 49.5,
          "en": "the object that is created behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 49.5,
          "end": 53.763,
          "en": "for this form here that is stored in this template variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 57.57,
          "en": "Therefore, if I wanna reset that form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.57,
          "end": 59.7,
          "en": "whenever the form is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.7,
          "end": 64.35,
          "en": "I could pass that form template variable as a third argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.35,
          "end": 65.493,
          "en": "to onSubmit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.63,
          "end": 70.68,
          "en": "And in the onSubmit method, I now just have to accept it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.68,
          "end": 73.2,
          "en": "and accept a form parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.2,
          "end": 74.973,
          "en": "which is of type HTMLFormElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.27,
          "end": 81.48,
          "en": "And then we could use this form parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.48,
          "end": 84.12,
          "en": "to call the built-in reset method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.12,
          "end": 87.66,
          "en": "on that HTMLFormElement object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.66,
          "end": 91.41,
          "en": "Because the object that's automatically constructed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "by the browser in the end for this form element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 98.16,
          "en": "does have such a reset method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.16,
          "end": 99.96000000000001,
          "en": "which does what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.96000000000001,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "It clears all the input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 105.63,
          "en": "that are inside of that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.63,
          "end": 109.473,
          "en": "So in this case, this input and this textarea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 111.18,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "Therefore with this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 116.67,
          "en": "if I save that and I go back to my application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.67,
          "end": 120.63,
          "en": "if I enter something here and I click submit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.63,
          "end": 123.54,
          "en": "you see those inputs are cleared thereafter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 123.54,
          "end": 126.753,
          "en": "and that happens because of form.reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.07,
          "end": 130.11,
          "en": "Now that's nice to know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.11,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "but that's not the main thing I want to show you here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 137.43,
          "en": "Instead, it would be nice if we could add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.43,
          "end": 139.77,
          "en": "that template variable here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 139.77,
          "end": 142.26,
          "en": "and then get hold of it inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.26,
          "end": 144,
          "en": "of that new ticket component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144,
          "end": 148.23,
          "en": "without passing it as an argument to onSubmit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.23,
          "end": 152.01,
          "en": "so that we don't have to pass all the things we wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.01,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "in onSubmit as an argument to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "Of course we can do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 158.25,
          "en": "but I wanna show you an alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.25,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "and that alternative can especially be helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 164.57999999999998,
          "en": "if you wanna access an element that has a template variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 164.57999999999998,
          "end": 169.07999999999998,
          "en": "on it in some code that's not triggered because of an event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.07999999999998,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "so where you can't pass the template variable easily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 174.813,
          "en": "as an argument to some method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 176.04,
          "end": 177.69,
          "en": "So to simulate that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.69,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "I'll remove form as an argument from onSubmit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 186.06,
          "en": "and I no longer expect to get it here as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.06,
          "end": 187.98,
          "en": "And therefore of course here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.98,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "form now is undefined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 195.15,
          "en": "or can't be found by JavaScript in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 198.543,
          "en": "because there is no variable called form available here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 199.82999999999998,
          "end": 202.8,
          "en": "But there now is a different way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.8,
          "end": 204.93,
          "en": "of that element in the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 207.273,
          "en": "that has this template variable on it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 208.68,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "We can get hold of it by adding a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 213.6,
          "en": "to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.6,
          "end": 215.43,
          "en": "For example, a property called form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.43,
          "end": 217.653,
          "en": "but the name is up to you of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.49,
          "end": 221.73,
          "en": "and by then decorating this property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 224.57999999999998,
          "en": "with the ViewChild decorator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.57999999999998,
          "end": 228.09300000000002,
          "en": "which must be imported from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 230.88,
          "end": 235.44,
          "en": "Now the ViewChild decorator is a decorator that can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 235.44,
          "end": 240.36,
          "en": "to select elements in the template of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 240.36,
          "end": 243.603,
          "en": "and make them available here in this component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 244.599,
          "end": 246.3,
          "en": "ViewChild therefore is a decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 246.3,
          "end": 250.56,
          "en": "that helps us find child elements in that component's view,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 250.56,
          "end": 252.663,
          "en": "so in that component's template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 253.68,
          "end": 258.68,
          "en": "To do that, ViewChild needs a selector as an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.16,
          "end": 264.75,
          "en": "and that selector can be a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.75,
          "end": 267.48,
          "en": "and I'll show you what to put into that string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.48,
          "end": 269.46,
          "en": "in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 269.46,
          "end": 272.28,
          "en": "But it could also be the class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 272.28,
          "end": 275.823,
          "en": "of one of your Components like ButtonComponent for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 279.87,
          "en": "If you would use such a class name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.87,
          "end": 283.02,
          "en": "then ViewChild would look for an instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 283.02,
          "end": 285.93,
          "en": "of your ButtonComponent in this template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 285.93,
          "end": 287.793,
          "en": "and here it would find one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 288.65999999999997,
          "end": 291.78,
          "en": "and it would then store that instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.78,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "in that form property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "So then you could interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 298.17,
          "en": "with that ButtonComponent instance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 298.17,
          "end": 302.4,
          "en": "via that property in this component class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 302.4,
          "end": 304.533,
          "en": "And that can sometimes be useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 305.52,
          "end": 308.73,
          "en": "You can also not just pass component classes here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 308.73,
          "end": 310.8,
          "en": "but also classes of Directives,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 310.8,
          "end": 313.053,
          "en": "but that's not something we need to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 314.19,
          "end": 318.84,
          "en": "Instead, another pretty powerful way of using ViewChild",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 318.84,
          "end": 323.04,
          "en": "is to pass a string to it and as a string value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 323.04,
          "end": 326.85,
          "en": "you pass one of your template variable names.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.85,
          "end": 328.623,
          "en": "So for example, form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.12,
          "end": 333.33,
          "en": "you can't pass a CSS selector here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.33,
          "end": 335.46,
          "en": "so something like that won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.46,
          "end": 338.61,
          "en": "You can't select elements by CSS class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.61,
          "end": 342.03,
          "en": "but you can pass the name of a template variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 345.65999999999997,
          "en": "So by passing form here without the hashtag,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 345.65999999999997,
          "end": 349.14,
          "en": "I'm telling Angular that it should look for an element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 349.14,
          "end": 351.813,
          "en": "with a template variable called form on it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.68,
          "end": 355.35,
          "en": "and then it should store the value that's stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.35,
          "end": 359.37,
          "en": "in that template variable or the value of the element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 359.37,
          "end": 361.86,
          "en": "on which this template variable is placed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 365.82,
          "en": "therefore in that property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.82,
          "end": 368.25,
          "en": "That's how that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 368.25,
          "end": 372.99,
          "en": "With that, you then just have to tell TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 372.99,
          "end": 376.26,
          "en": "which type of value will actually be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.26,
          "end": 377.673,
          "en": "in that property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.54,
          "end": 381.99,
          "en": "and that would be an ElementRef.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.99,
          "end": 385.83,
          "en": "So you must import ElementRef from angular/core",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 385.83,
          "end": 388.953,
          "en": "and use that as a type for this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 390.27,
          "end": 394.23,
          "en": "Now the ElementRef type just defines the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 394.23,
          "end": 397.26,
          "en": "for a wrapper object though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 397.26,
          "end": 401.37,
          "en": "Because Angular in the end will wrap the element it finds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 401.37,
          "end": 405.45,
          "en": "with help of that selector in such an ElementRef object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 405.45,
          "end": 408.65999999999997,
          "en": "and that's why ElementRef is actually a generic type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.65999999999997,
          "end": 412.23,
          "en": "that needs extra information about the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 412.23,
          "end": 416.4,
          "en": "that will be wrapped by it here when using ViewChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 416.4,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "So you give it that extra information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 420.51,
          "en": "by adding angle brackets here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 420.51,
          "end": 422.22,
          "en": "and then between those angle brackets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 422.22,
          "end": 424.44,
          "en": "you define the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 424.44,
          "end": 426.613,
          "en": "that will be wrapped by ElementRef,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 426.613,
          "end": 428.516,
          "en": "which will be the type of value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 428.516,
          "end": 430.809,
          "en": "that will be selected by that selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 430.809,
          "end": 434.58,
          "en": "so the type of element that will be selected by it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 434.58,
          "end": 435.72,
          "en": "And here in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 435.72,
          "end": 438.243,
          "en": "that will be an HTMLFormElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 439.903,
          "end": 442.38,
          "en": "so that is the type that should go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 442.38,
          "end": 443.943,
          "en": "between these angle brackets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 445.77,
          "end": 449.37,
          "en": "Last but not least, you should add a question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 449.37,
          "end": 451.14,
          "en": "because this property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 451.14,
          "end": 454.77,
          "en": "will not immediately be populated with a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 454.77,
          "end": 459,
          "en": "Instead, when this component class here is instantiated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 459,
          "end": 461.22,
          "en": "no template will exist yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 461.22,
          "end": 464.7,
          "en": "because Angular won't have initialized it yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 464.7,
          "end": 466.5,
          "en": "And therefore initially,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 466.5,
          "end": 470.76,
          "en": "this will indeed be undefined and it will only be populated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 470.76,
          "end": 474.933,
          "en": "with the value once Angular has initialized the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 476.1,
          "end": 479.43,
          "en": "That's why for example in the constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 479.43,
          "end": 483.84,
          "en": "you would not be able to access this form element yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 483.84,
          "end": 486,
          "en": "but that's no problem because we need access",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 486,
          "end": 487.89,
          "en": "to it here in onSubmit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 487.89,
          "end": 491.97,
          "en": "and we can now get access here by using this.form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 491.97,
          "end": 493.653,
          "en": "so by using this property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 494.55,
          "end": 497.01,
          "en": "And now we just need to convince TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 497.01,
          "end": 502.01,
          "en": "that this will be defined so that it will not be undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 502.47,
          "end": 505.53,
          "en": "And you can do that by adding a question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 505.53,
          "end": 508.26,
          "en": "which tells TypeScript that it should only try",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 508.26,
          "end": 513.26,
          "en": "to access the reset method if this here is not undefined,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 513.45,
          "end": 515.55,
          "en": "otherwise it will not continue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 515.55,
          "end": 518.433,
          "en": "so that it won't generate a runtime error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 519.45,
          "end": 521.28,
          "en": "Now I'm still getting an error here though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 521.28,
          "end": 523.77,
          "en": "that reset does not exist on the type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 523.77,
          "end": 525.33,
          "en": "because inside of the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 525.33,
          "end": 528.993,
          "en": "we stored that ElementRef object, not the HTMLFormElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 530.01,
          "end": 533.28,
          "en": "Instead that is wrapped by this ElementRef object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 533.28,
          "end": 537.42,
          "en": "So we first need to access the nativeElement property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 537.42,
          "end": 539.82,
          "en": "on that ElementRef wrapper object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 539.82,
          "end": 543,
          "en": "and that will then be that HTMLFormElement,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 543,
          "end": 545.583,
          "en": "so there we can then call reset.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 547.11,
          "end": 549.93,
          "en": "And that's there for a different way of getting hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 549.93,
          "end": 554.07,
          "en": "of an element that is stored in the template inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 554.07,
          "end": 556.05,
          "en": "of this component class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 556.05,
          "end": 558.483,
          "en": "with help of the ViewChild decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 559.35,
          "end": 562.5,
          "en": "With that, if you save everything and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 562.5,
          "end": 564.36,
          "en": "you'll see that if you submit the form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 564.36,
          "end": 567.273,
          "en": "it is still reset as it was before.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
